Subject: [PATCH] fix: persist locked portraits to disk, restore on restart
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

main.py:
- PORTRAITS_FILE = /app/master_portraits.json — loaded on startup
- load_master_portraits() / save_master_portraits() helpers
- set_master_portrait now calls save_master_portraits() immediately
- GET /locked-personas — list all locked personas with fal URLs
- DELETE /locked-personas/{persona_id} — remove a lock

static/index.html:
- On init: fetch /locked-personas and restore masterPortraitUrl to
  matching personas (backend is source of truth, survives restarts)
- renderPortraitStep: show locked UI when masterPortraitUrl set,
  not only when loraUrl set. Shows reference photo in comparison panel
- genPortraitWithLora: works with masterPortraitUrl fallback, not
  only loraUrl. Sends master_url + persona_id to portrait endpoint

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
